MODE      cm-threads-switch
FORMS     0x26 0x27 0x28 0x29 0x2a 0x2b 0x2c 0x2d  (all eight 🧵 phase-1 productions)
RESULT    143165567  (0x0888887f)
EXIT      0
RUNS      2, byte-identical

PACKING   bits 0-5 the marker mask; then six 4-bit thread.index values — the entry Thread at
          bit 6, then the five bodies in creation order at 10, 14, 18, 22, 26. 30 bits of 32.

MASK      0b111111 — every marker set
  bit 1   thread.index                (0x26) — the entry Thread recorded its own index
  bit 2   thread.suspend-then-resume  (0x2a) — body ran, resumed the suspended switcher
  bit 4   thread.yield-then-resume    (0x2b) — body ran, switcher stayed ready
  bit 8   thread.suspend-then-promote (0x2c) — body ran after resume-later made it READY
  bit 16  thread.yield-then-promote   (0x2d) — body ran after resume-later made it READY
  bit 32  thread.suspend              (0x29) — body ran and resumed the suspended switcher

INDICES
  entry                      1
  body k=0 suspend-then-resume   2
  body k=1 yield-then-resume     2
  body k=2 suspend-then-promote  2
  body k=3 yield-then-promote    2
  body k=4 plain suspend         2
  Every body is 2, and that is the measurement rather than an artefact: each body returns and
  UNREGISTERS before the next is created, so `inst.threads` frees the slot and the next Thread
  reuses it. An implementation that numbered Threads monotonically would read 2,3,4,5,6 here and
  would set every marker bit while being wrong about observable guest state.

WHAT THIS READING PINS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
  Pinned:     the mask (reachability of each production) and the six index values.
  NOT pinned: the ORDER in which ready Threads run. The reference schedules them
              nondeterministically — `Store.tick` picks `random.choice(list(candidates))` from the
              ready set — so an order is not a property of a conforming implementation. The mask is
              an OR and is order-independent by construction; the indices are each written by their
              own body and do not depend on order either. A witness built on this reading must
              assert these values and must not assert an execution order.

OUTCOME   task.return(143165567) then EXIT (code 0); the call completed

GATE OFF
  `thread.resume-later` requires the component model threading feature (at offset 0x47)
  exit 1 — a parse refusal naming the first 🧵 production in the canon section

BURROUGHS
  burroughs: feature not implemented in this phase: component: canon 0: canon thread.resume-later
  (0x28) is a shared-everything-threads built-in, which this engine does not support — the
  component is well-formed and no gate admits this proposal
  exit 5 — refused by name, the same production wasmtime names

NOT MEASURED
  Whether an instance is usable after a 🧵 trap. `wasmtime run` instantiates afresh for each
  invocation, so re-entry after a trap is not observable through this harness, and no fixture for
  it was built.

